  "answer":"The production checklist’s limit refers to the metric thresholds that must be met before a model can be promoted to production. According to the Release Policy, a model change must show an improvement of at least 0.005 in F1 score and the ROC‑AUC may not drop by more than 0.01 on the frozen holdout evaluation set. These are the limits you would adjust if you wanted to change the checklist criteria.",
  "sources":[
    {
      "source_id":"release-policy",
      "quote":"Production model changes require an evaluation on a frozen holdout. Promote only when F1 improves by at least 0.005 and ROC-AUC drops by no more than 0.01."
    }
  ]
}
